 enum values were interpreted by splitting at the last dot, which treats an enum name as a class name. As a result, `[constant MyEnum.VALUE]` could open repeated Unknown Help Class tabs, and duplicate value names in different enums could not be linked independently.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThis resolves member links against documented class prefixes while preserving enum-qualified constant names, and adds `Enum.VALUE` and `Class.Enum.VALUE` entries to the help page's constant lookup table. It also preserves global enum and nested script class links.\r\n\r\nTested with a Windows x86_64 dev editor built from this commit:\r\n\r\n- `prek` on `editor/doc/editor_help.cpp`\r\n- `scons platform=windows target=editor dev_build=yes accesskit=no d3d12=no -j8`\r\n- Runtime clicks for same-class and cross-class `Enum.VALUE`, `Class.VALUE`, and `Class.Enum.VALUE`\r\n- Two named enums sharing `VALUE`, each reaching its own paragraph\r\n- Class-qualified method, member, signal, enum, and ordinary constant links\r\n- `Variant.Type.TYPE_NIL` in `@GlobalScope`\r\n- Nested script class links from both inside and outside the outer class\r\n\r\n> [!INFO] *AI disclosure*: This contribution was authored by an autonomous OpenAI Codex agent on behalf of @AvaloNero. Claude Code was used as an independent reviewer of the implementation, issue conversation, test evidence, and pull request description.","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6051509301,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaLK0NQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/spam","name":"spam","description":"","color":"E94A26","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":"spam","created_at":"2026-08-13T19:32:56Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T13:03:30Z","cl